{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the neurology doctors. You're here because of a severe headache. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:37:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I woke up this morning with the worst headache—pounding, pressure, like my head is swelling. It’s in both temples. I’ve had migraines before, but this one wouldn’t go away with Tylenol or even Ativan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any sensitivity to light or sound? Nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:39:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, both. And I’ve been nauseous, not eating much. Also, I’ve had sharp stabbing pain in my right eye—just for seconds at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That can happen with migraines. Any vision changes, weakness, or trouble speaking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:42:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, but since I got to the ER, my right forearm and hand have been tingling. That’s new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:43:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, we’ll check that. Your blood pressure is quite high—200 over 110. That could be from pain or stress. We’ll monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I’m on meds for that, but it’s been hard to keep it down when I’m in pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:46:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure your medications are adjusted. You mentioned you were just discharged about 10 days ago for a similar issue?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:47:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I was on steroids and they helped a lot. But I stopped them five days ago, and now the headaches are back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That might be part of it. Sometimes when steroids are tapered quickly, headaches can rebound. We’re going to restart IV steroids to see if that helps again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:50:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. But I’m worried—could this be something more serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your exam is reassuring. No signs of stroke or nerve damage. The tingling is likely part of the migraine aura. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:53:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m also allergic to NSAIDs and Motrin, so I can’t take those."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2140-09-07 21:54:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Noted. We’ll avoid those. We’re giving you IV fluids and Zofran for nausea. The IV steroid should start helping soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2140-09-08 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the headache today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2140-09-08 07:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better this morning—much less pressure. But it came back a little this afternoon yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2140-09-08 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. The steroids help, but we may need a longer-term plan. We spoke with your headache specialist, Dr. Patel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2140-09-08 07:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, good. I’ve been seeing her at the Headache Center."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2140-09-08 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "She agrees we should try Depakote, since Topamax and amitriptyline were stopped. It’s safer for you now that you’re off Topamax and have a history of kidney stones."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2140-09-08 07:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember—Topamax caused stones before. Is Depakote safe with my liver and diabetes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2140-09-08 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your labs—liver and blood sugar are stable. We’ll start with a low dose and monitor. You’ll take it at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2140-09-08 07:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds okay. What about the tingling? It’s still there, off and on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2140-09-08 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still no weakness or other changes. It’s likely sensory aura from migraine. But we’ll keep watching."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2140-09-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you one dose of IV Depakote this morning. You’ll start the pill tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2140-09-08 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Did it help at all?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2140-09-08 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You said the headache was less intense this afternoon. That’s a good sign. We’re also adjusting your blood pressure meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2140-09-08 10:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought my BP meds were okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2140-09-08 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re lowering your amlodipine dose and increasing propranolol back to 120 mg. It helps both BP and migraines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2140-09-08 10:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on 120 before. Is it safe now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2140-09-08 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and it may help prevent future headaches. We’re also giving you Midrin for breakthrough pain—safe with your allergies."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2140-09-08 10:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’ve been so stressed lately—my mom has Alzheimer’s, and I’m her caregiver. I think that’s making the headaches worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2140-09-08 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stress is a major trigger. We’ve asked social work to meet with you. They can help connect you with support groups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2140-09-08 10:13:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d really appreciate that. I feel so alone sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2140-09-08 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You met with social work this morning, right? How did that go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2140-09-08 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, they were so kind. Gave me info on an Alzheimer’s support group and a bereavement group—my dad passed last year."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2140-09-08 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad. Emotional support is part of your treatment. Dr. Patel also mentioned they’re reconsidering a shunt for your intracranial pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2140-09-08 14:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought they said I didn’t need one?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2140-09-08 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because your pressures have varied and headaches keep coming back, they want to re-evaluate. It’s not urgent, but an option."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2140-09-09 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well overnight. Headache much better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2140-09-09 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, still some pressure, but manageable. I haven’t needed extra meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2140-09-09 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re going to discharge you today with Depakote at night and Midrin as needed. Keep following up with Dr. Patel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2140-09-09 08:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure and diabetes meds are adjusted?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2140-09-09 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—amlodipine 5 mg twice daily, propranolol back to 120 mg, and the rest as before. Watch for dizziness or low blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2140-09-09 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll call if I get numbness, vision changes, or the headache gets bad again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2140-09-09 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And keep in touch with social work for therapy. You’ve made progress—both physically and emotionally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2140-09-09 08:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel hopeful for the first time in weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2140-09-09 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2140-09-09 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before discharge. Any new symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2140-09-09 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, still the same mild tingling, but it’s not worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2140-09-09 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Neuro exam is still normal. You’re cleared to go home with your prescriptions and instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2140-09-09 10:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I really appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2140-09-09 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Stay in touch with your team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2140-09-09 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your discharge papers now, including when to follow up with Dr. Patel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2140-09-09 12:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make that appointment right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2140-09-09 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care, and we’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2140-09-07 21:36:00",
    "admission_end": "2140-09-09 15:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of migraines, pseudotumor cerebri, hypertension, diabetes, and depression was readmitted two days after a prior discharge due to recurrence of severe bifrontal headaches with photophobia, phonophobia, nausea, and new right forearm and hand paresthesias. Her symptoms began shortly after completing a steroid taper, and initial management included IV methylprednisolone, which provided partial relief. Given the recurrence and limitations in medication options due to NSAID allergies and prior kidney stone risk, the treatment plan was adjusted in consultation with her headache specialist to include IV and then oral Depakote for migraine prophylaxis and Midrin for breakthrough pain. Propranolol was increased back to 120 mg daily, and amlodipine was reduced. Social work was consulted, and the patient engaged in supportive counseling, identifying stress and caregiving responsibilities as significant contributors to her condition. She improved clinically, was discharged home with close follow-up, and is being reconsidered for a shunt due to fluctuating intracranial pressures.",
    "problems": [
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Benign intracranial hypertension",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of aspirin"
    ]
  }
}
